 "rationale": "The open-circuit voltage of the piezo is too low (0.76V) to reach the 1.8V target with a passive rectifier. Parallel Synchronous Switch Harvesting on Inductor (P-SSHI) uses an inductor and a switch to flip the voltage across the piezo capacitance at the peaks, effectively increasing the voltage seen by the rectifier. A Zener clamp is added to keep vout below 3.6V.",
